# bolt — lift-source, and the source is OUR OWN main

Upstream: NONE. conda-forge packages no LLVM BOLT.
Lift from:  NAGAGroup/acpp-toolchain, branch main
Pinned:     22bf38e00d9f66688f560ef995852c3c35bd4b40

RULING (Research Lead, 2026-09-05, overruling my recommendation to drop it):
BOLT is not merely built today, it is SHIPPED. Dropping a currently-shipped
binary because conda-forge has no feedstock for it would let packaging
convenience decide product shape, which is precisely the failure this rebuild
exists to end.

VERIFIED AT SOURCE, not taken on trust:
  * main:release/recipe.yaml lines 1010-1013 and 1246-1249 — bin/llvm-bolt,
    bin/llvm-bolt-heatmap, bin/perf2bolt, bin/merge-fdata are INCLUDE globs in
    the acpp-tools output (they sit in the same list as bin/clang-tidy,
    bin/clangd, bin/scan-build).
  * main:release/recipe.yaml line 1360-1363 — acpp-tools' package_contents
    test asserts llvm-bolt exists, gated `if: linux` with the comment 'bolt is
    ELF-only; it does not build on win'.
  * main:shared/build-stage.nu line 240 — the linux configure passes
    -DLLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS=clang;lld;lldb;clang-tools-extra;bolt;polly;openmp.
    The win branch (line 338) and the mac branch (line 94) do not, and line 87
    records why for mac: bolt has no darwin port.

SO WHAT THE NEW RECIPE MUST DO: keep the four bolt binaries in acpp-tools, and
express their absence on win and osx as a `skip:`/conditional inside a UNIFORM
output list — never by dropping the output or silently omitting the globs,
which is the variation-by-omission defect being fixed.

WHAT WE LIFT: the LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS entry, the four output globs and the
platform gating, all from main. There is no upstream recipe, no upstream
patches and no upstream flags to inherit, so this lift's provenance is our own
history and the PINNED_REF above is a commit in THIS repo.

TO SEE THE LIFT:
    git show 22bf38e:release/recipe.yaml
    git show 22bf38e:shared/build-stage.nu
